</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>G protein-coupled receptor dimerisation: Molecular basis and relevance to function</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><year>2007</year><volume>1768</volume><fpage>825</fpage><lpage>835</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17069751</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.bbamem.2006.09.021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jastrzebska</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Maeda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Fotiadis</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Filipek</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Stenkamp</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Palczewski</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional characterization of rhodopsin monomers and dimers in detergents</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2004</year><volume>279</volume><fpage>54663</fpage><lpage>54675</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15489507</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.M408691200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bettler</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Oliveira</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Campagne</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><surname>Vriend</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GPCRDB information system for G protein-coupled receptors</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>294</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12520006</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/gkg103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edvardsen</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Reiersen</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Beukers</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kristiansen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>tGRAP, the G-protein coupled receptors mutant database</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>361</fpage><lpage>363</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11752337</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/30.1.361</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fleming</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Engelman</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specificity in transmembrane helix-helix interactions can define a hierarchy of stability for sequence variants</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>14340</fpage><lpage>14344</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11724930</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.251367498</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pin</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Neubig</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouvier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Devi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Filizola</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Javitch</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lohse</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Milligan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Palczewski</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Parmentier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Spedding</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>International Union of Basic and Clinical Pharmacology. LXVII. Recommendations for the recognition and nomenclature of G protein-coupled receptor heteromultimers</article-title><source>Pharmacol Rev</source><year>2007</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17329545</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1124/pr.59.1.5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Weare</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Beukers</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Horsch</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bairoch</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Edvardsen</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Campagne</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Vriend</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GPCRDB: an information system for G protein-coupled receptors</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>279</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9399852</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/26.1.275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ponder</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><arti